.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH verify 1  "verify " 
.SH NAME
verify \- Verify signed blocks in an HTML file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBverify\fR [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-ignore\-tls\-errors\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE|URL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Locate every block carrying a data\-hs\-signature attribute, recompute its
canonical bytes, and check the embedded ML\-DSA signature. The command exits
non\-zero if any block is invalid or, when a key is expected, mismatches it.
.PP
With \-k, every block must additionally be signed by exactly the given
public key — an armored key.pub or a .hskey secret key file (unlocked with
the passphrase) — defeating re\-signing of altered content.
.PP
When FILE is an http:// or https:// URL, the document is fetched over
HTTPS (validating the TLS certificate unless \-\-ignore\-tls\-errors is given)
and the signing key is resolved from the _hs_key.<host> DNS pin record,
downloading the key and checking its SHA3\-256 fingerprint against the pin.
.PP
\-\-format json emits a machine\-readable report (ok, total, verified, key
origin, and per\-block results) instead of the human\-readable text report.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Restrict verification to a specific public key.

Accepts either an armored public key file (`key.pub`) or a `.hskey` secret key file (unlocked with the passphrase).
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-tls\-errors\fR
Skip TLS certificate validation when verifying a URL
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: text]
Output format: text (default) or json
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
text: Human\-readable text report
.IP \(bu 2
json: Machine\-readable JSON report
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-passphrase\fR
Use an empty passphrase (no prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fI<PASSPHRASE_FILE>\fR
Read the passphrase from a file (first line)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE|URL\fR>
HTML file or URL to verify
